Can you just use a session-level density covariate for food? Or perhaps include a larger-scale food covariate measured at the pixel level? I wouldn't put too much emphasis on the significantly negative relationship at the more fine scale because the effect size is negligible and I believe these models will overestimate precision in practice when there is likely some residual non-compensatory individual heterogeneity and extra Poisson variation in density.

Ben

