Hello,

Yes, I could use a session-level density covariate, that is an option. I just lose quite a bit of power/resolution that way, as opposed to doing it at the mask and home range centre level.

Even if the precision is over estimated, and it is not significantly negative, and just a flat line, I still find it surprising how different the results could be.

Cheers,
Clayton

